IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-nouns`
IMPORT `spr-part1-general`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 5 (Amendments to other legislation): regulation 14 and the Schedule.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- Part 5 is the one Part that regulation 1(3) does not switch off for a person who reached pensionable age before
-- 6 April 2016, so nothing here is gated on that.
-- The Schedule is almost entirely amending machinery (insert a word, renumber a regulation, add a definition) in two other
-- sets of Regulations that are not among the inputs; those paragraphs are `inert` in NOTES.md with their reasons.
-- What decides something for a person is the regulation 6 that paragraph 1(10) inserts into the Sharing of State Scheme
-- Rights (Provision of Information and Valuation) (No.2) Regulations 2000: what the Secretary of State must furnish to a
-- person with shareable new state scheme rights (or to their spouse or civil partner, or to a court), and by when.
-- That is encoded below. "Shareable new state scheme rights" (section 47(3) of the 1999 Act) and "the relevant date"
-- (section 10(3) of the Family Law (Scotland) Act 1985) are borrowed terms, taken as facts.

§ `Part 5 -- Amendments to other legislation`

§§ `Schedule, paragraph 1(10): inserted regulation 6(1) to (6): what the Secretary of State must furnish`

-- (2) to (5): which valuation (and amount) the information consists of. (6): the explanation, always.
-- src:550 | (2) Except where paragraphs (3) or (4) apply, the information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's shareable new state scheme rights as at the date of receipt of a request for such a valuation.
-- src:551 | (3) The information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date, where the relevant date is on or after 6th April 2016.
-- src:552 | (4) The information specified in this paragraph is a valuation of the person's previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date, where the relevant date is before 6th April 2016 and the request for a valuation is received on or after 6th April 2016.
-- src:553 | (5) The information specified in this paragraph is the amount of the person's former entitlement to a category A retirement pension by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act as at the relevant date and immediately before 6th April 2016, where the relevant date is before 6th April 2016 and the request for information about that amount is received on or after 6th April 2016.
-- src:554 | (6) The information in this paragraph is an explanation of—
-- src:555 | (a) the shareable new state scheme rights;
-- src:556 | (b) how a pension sharing order or provision will affect a person's shareable new state scheme rights;
-- src:557 | (c) how a pension sharing order or provision in respect of a person's shareable new state scheme rights will result in the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights becoming entitled to an amount because of a new state scheme pension credit; and
-- src:558 | (d) how any amount in sub-paragraph (c) differs from an amount of shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(2), 6(3), 6(4), 6(5), 6(6) (src:550-558)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for information about sharing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the valuation is as at the relevant date and the relevant date is on or after 6 April 2016` `the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the request`'s `the relevant date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `a relevant date` THEN Day `a relevant date` AT LEAST Day `the date the Regulations come into force`

@ref Inserted regulation 6(4), 6(5) (src:552-553)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for information about sharing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the relevant date is before 6 April 2016 and the request is received on or after it` `the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the request`'s `the relevant date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `a relevant date` THEN
            Day `a relevant date` LESS THAN Day `the date the Regulations come into force`
        AND Day (`the request`'s `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order`) AT LEAST Day `the date the Regulations come into force`

-- The valuations and amount that go with a request that includes one (paragraphs (2) to (5)).
@ref Inserted regulation 6(2), 6(3), 6(4), 6(5) (src:550-553)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for information about sharing`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Item of information about sharing`
`the valuations and amount that go with the request` `the request` MEANS
    IF   `the valuation is as at the relevant date and the relevant date is on or after 6 April 2016` `the request`
    THEN LIST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
    ELSE IF   `the relevant date is before 6 April 2016 and the request is received on or after it` `the request`
         THEN LIST `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`, `the amount of the former entitlement to a category A retirement pension by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act, as at the relevant date and immediately before 6 April 2016`
         ELSE LIST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`

-- src:545 | (1) The requirements imposed on the Secretary of State for the purposes of section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act (supply of pension information in connection with divorce etc.) are that he shall furnish—
-- src:546 | (a) the information specified in paragraphs (2) to (6)—
-- src:547 | (i) to a person who has shareable new state scheme rights on request from that person; or
-- src:548 | (ii) to the court, pursuant to an order of the court; or
-- src:549 | (b) the information specified in paragraph (6) to the spouse or civil partner of a person who has shareable new state scheme rights, on request from that spouse or civil partner.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(1)(a) (src:545-549)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for information about sharing`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Item of information about sharing`
`the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` `the request` MEANS
    IF   `the request`'s `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)`
    THEN append (`the valuations and amount that go with the request` `the request`) (LIST `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`)
    ELSE LIST `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`

-- Paragraph (1)(b): the spouse or civil partner is owed the explanation in paragraph (6) only.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(1)(b) (src:549)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Item of information about sharing`
`the information the spouse or civil partner of the person is owed on request` MEANS
    LIST `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`

§§ `Schedule, paragraph 1(10): inserted regulation 6(7) and (8): by when`

-- (7): within three months beginning with the day the request or order is received; six weeks if the person has notified the
-- Secretary of State that the information is needed in connection with proceedings; or such shorter period as the court
-- specifies. The list is read as "the earliest that applies" (fork F13): otherwise (b) and (c) would never bite.
-- (8): where the request does not include a valuation or amount, or the spouse asks for the explanation, within one month.
-- "Beginning with" counts the first day as day one (fork F7): six weeks beginning with the day of receipt end 41 days later.
-- src:559 | (7) The Secretary of State shall furnish the information specified in paragraphs (2) to (6) to the court, or, as the case may be, to the person who has shareable new state scheme rights within—
-- src:560 | (a) three months beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or, as the case may be, the order for the provision of that information;
-- src:561 | (b) six weeks beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or, as the case may be, the order for the provision of the information, if the person who has shareable new state scheme rights has notified the Secretary of State by the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order that the information is needed in connection with proceedings commenced under any of the provisions referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act; or
-- src:562 | (c) such shorter period specified by the court in an order requiring the Secretary of State to provide a valuation in accordance with paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount in accordance with paragraph (5).
-- src:563 | (8) Where—
-- src:564 | (a) the request made by the person with shareable new state scheme rights for, or the court order requiring, the provision of information does not include a request or, as the case may be, an order for a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5); or
-- src:565 | (b) the spouse or civil partner of the person with shareable new state scheme rights requests the information specified in paragraph (6),
-- src:566 | the Secretary of State shall furnish that information to the person who has shareable new state scheme rights, that person's spouse or civil partner, or the court, as the case may be, within one month beginning with the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the court order for the provision of that information.
@ref Inserted regulation 6(7), 6(8) (src:559-566)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request for information about sharing`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` `the request` MEANS
    IF   `the request`'s `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)`
    THEN Date (minimum (append `the three months` (append `the six weeks` `the courts period`)))
    ELSE `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` `the day it is received`
    WHERE
        `the day it is received` MEANS `the request`'s `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order`
        `the three months` MEANS LIST Day (`the last day of a period of` 3 `months starting on` `the day it is received`)
        `the six weeks` MEANS
            IF   `the request`'s `the person notified the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings`
            THEN LIST (Day `the day it is received` PLUS 41)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the courts period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the request`'s `the last day of a shorter period specified by the court in an order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST `the courts last day` THEN LIST Day `the courts last day`
